Types of Saga
1. Choreography Saga

Each service publishes events.

Other services listen and continue processing.

Order Service

↓

Order Created Event

↓

Payment Service

↓

Payment Success Event

↓

Inventory Service

↓

Inventory Reserved Event

↓

Notification Service

Advantages

No central coordinator
Simple for small systems

Disadvantages

Harder to understand as the number of services grows
Event flow can become complex
2. Orchestration Saga

A central orchestrator controls the workflow.

Saga Orchestrator

      │

      ▼

Order Service

      ▼

Payment Service

      ▼

Inventory Service

      ▼

Shipping Service

      ▼

Notification Service

Advantages

Easier to monitor and debug
Better for complex business processes

Disadvantages

Requires an orchestrator component
Spring Boot Example
Account Service
@Transactional
public void debit(Long accountId, double amount) {

    // Debit account
}
Compensation
@Transactional
public void credit(Long accountId, double amount) {

    // Reverse debit
}

The orchestrator invokes credit() if a later step fails.

