Saga vs Two-Phase Commit (2PC)
Saga Pattern	Two-Phase Commit (2PC)
Local transactions	Global transaction
Uses compensation	Uses commit/rollback across all participants
High scalability	Lower scalability
Preferred for microservices	More common in tightly coupled distributed systems
Eventually consistent	Strongly consistent